WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:05.377
Ally and Mateo arrived at the museum at the same time.

2
00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:11.132
They raced for the main entrance, but a security guard blocked the doorway.

3
00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:14.604
"Press passes, please," he demanded.

4
00:00:14.605 --> 00:00:18.842
Ally had no idea what he was talking about, but she blurted out a reply.

5
00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:23.385
"We don't have those. But we need to hear what Lainie Polk says!"

6
00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:27.671
"You'll hear about it in the news like everyone else."

7
00:00:27.672 --> 00:00:32.808
The guard closed the door, shutting them out of the museum.

8
00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:40.419
Ally sighed. "I guess we have to go home and wait for the news to be released."

9
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.567
"No, we are not giving up!" Mateo was adamant.

10
00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:48.495
"I'm going to see if I can find another way in. Wait here."

11
00:00:48.496 --> 00:00:56.036
As Ally sat down on a bench to wait for Mateo to return, she spotted the customer from the diner who'd caught the cupcake tray.

12
00:00:56.037 --> 00:00:58.344
She was heading for the entrance.

13
00:00:58.345 --> 00:01:01.577
"I should warn her about the press passes," Ally thought.

14
00:01:01.578 --> 00:01:10.147
But before Ally could reach her, the customer whispered something to the security guard, who tipped his hat and let her in.

15
00:01:10.148 --> 00:01:15.314
Ally was stunned. "He didn't even ask her for a press pass!" she thought.

16
00:01:15.315 --> 00:01:21.988
"Maybe it's not my imagination. Maybe I was right, and she is a Carparian. Yikes!

17
00:01:21.989 --> 00:01:25.791
What if she's here on a mission to stop Lainie Polk's P.O.D.?"

18
00:01:25.792 --> 00:01:28.215
Now Ally really had to get inside!

19
00:01:28.216 --> 00:01:36.258
Mateo hurried over. "I found Phil. He's going to let us in a back door, right into the auditorium."

20
00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:40.490
"Thank goodness!" Ally told Mateo about her suspicions.

21
00:01:40.491 --> 00:01:47.261
"If that customer is a Carparian, I can guarantee you that she's not here to make peace!"

22
00:01:47.262 --> 00:01:51.052
*** Ally and Mateo took seats in the last row of the

23
00:01:51.053 --> 00:01:54.359
auditorium. Ally looked around for any sign of the

24
00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.482
Carparian. She was up front, talking to Dr. Cosmo

25
00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:02.487
Lloyd. "Could he know she's a Carparian?" Ally whispered to

26
00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:06.271
Mateo. "Or maybe she wants to kidnap him! I should do

27
00:02:06.272 --> 00:02:09.807
something!" She started to get up, but just then the lights

28
00:02:09.808 --> 00:02:13.154
dimmed. The press conference was about to

29
00:02:13.155 --> 00:02:16.841
begin. Dr. Lloyd stepped up to the

30
00:02:16.842 --> 00:02:20.169
microphone. "Thank you all for coming on such short

31
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:24.763
notice. The Sandville UFO Museum is honored to host this special

32
00:02:24.764 --> 00:02:29.538
event. And now please join me in welcoming Lainie Polk!"

33
00:02:29.539 --> 00:02:35.876
Everyone sat forward in their seats, eager to get a look at the mysterious billionaire.

34
00:02:35.877 --> 00:02:40.763
But instead of a person, a robot walked onto the stage.

35
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:45.838
"Welcome and thank you for coming." The robot spoke with a human-sounding voice.

36
00:02:45.839 --> 00:02:54.867
"Polk's Orbiting Device, otherwise known as P.O.D., has been engineered to fly beyond the Milky Way, into galaxies far, far away.

37
00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.450
And the adventure begins in two days."

38
00:02:57.451 --> 00:03:00.112
The reporters gasped in surprise.

39
00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:03.471
"Where is it launching from?" one asked.

40
00:03:03.472 --> 00:03:07.484
"That location will remain undisclosed," the robot replied.

41
00:03:07.485 --> 00:03:12.235
"Ms. Polk doesn't want anything, or anyone, to interfere with the launch."

42
00:03:12.236 --> 00:03:16.788
"What about passengers? Who will be onboard?" another reporter asked.

43
00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:21.814
"That is the reason Ms. Polk called this press conference," the robot replied.

44
00:03:21.815 --> 00:03:24.110
A hush fell over the auditorium.

45
00:03:24.111 --> 00:03:27.829
Everyone waited to hear what the robot would say next.

46
00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:32.266
"A piece of paper with a number has been taped to the bottom of your seat."

47
00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:36.240
"They're going to pick someone here!" Ally squealed.

48
00:03:36.241 --> 00:03:41.823
"Silence," the robot ordered. "I will run a program to pick a random number.

49
00:03:41.824 --> 00:03:46.042
The attendee with the winning number will get to fly with Ms. Polk on the P.O.D."

50
00:03:46.043 --> 00:03:52.329
Ally grabbed her number from beneath her seat. "Twenty-five. What's your number, Mateo?"

51
00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:57.401
"Twelve," he said. "But if the robot calls my number, I'm giving it to you."

52
00:03:57.402 --> 00:04:03.288
Ally was touched. "Are you sure? I know how badly you want to fly to space."

53
00:04:03.289 --> 00:04:08.983
"And I know how badly you want to get home." Mateo crossed his fingers for good luck.

54
00:04:08.984 --> 00:04:11.796
"I've already gotten lucky," Ally thought.

55
00:04:11.797 --> 00:04:18.244
"Lucky to have such a great friend. I'm going to miss him so much when I leave."

56
00:04:18.245 --> 00:04:21.416
"I will now select the winning number," the robot said.

57
00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:27.533
Suddenly Dr. Lloyd rushed back up to the microphone. "This is ridiculous!" he cried.

58
00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:31.440
"Lainie Polk should take a scientist with her on P.O.D.

59
00:04:31.441 --> 00:04:36.643
Someone who's dedicated his entire life to studying UFOs and alien life-forms.

60
00:04:36.644 --> 00:04:40.677
Someone . . . like me!"

61
00:04:40.678 --> 00:04:43.306
"Negative," the robot replied.

62
00:04:43.307 --> 00:04:47.829
"Lainie Polk will only take the winner of the lottery on P.O.D."

63
00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:54.958
The robot pressed a button on its control panel, and lights flashed.

64
00:04:54.959 --> 00:04:57.406
"The winning number has been chosen."

65
00:04:57.407 --> 00:05:06.418
"Oh please, please," Ally whispered softly. "Call number 25!"

